# Build context of the demo image (Dockerfile, DECISIONS.md D-035).
#
# Allow-list: everything is excluded, then only what the Dockerfile copies is let back in.
# A file added anywhere else in the repository later (a database, a key, a log, notes) stays
# out of the image without anyone having to remember to list it here.
*

!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/uv.lock
!backend/alembic.ini
!backend/alembic/
!backend/app/
!backend/seed/
!backend/scripts/
!frontend/

# Never, not even inside the allowed folders. The last matching rule wins, so these stay
# below the allow-list.
# Secrets and settings (the image gets its settings from compose, never from a .env file).
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Databases: the real ledger, demo files, WAL/SHM/journal side files, backups.
**/*.db*
**/*.sqlite*
# Trained models contain the symbols of the real holdings.
backend/artifacts/
**/artifacts/
# Version control, local tooling, notes.
.git
**/.git
.github/
.claude/
**/.claude
docs/
deploy/
**/.vscode
**/.idea
# Dependencies and build output are produced inside the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Tests, caches, logs.
backend/tests/
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.vitest
**/*.log
